# Alt-Help held down, then pressed again, while its screen dump runs. TOS
# adds one to _dumpflg at each Alt-Help, the held key's repeats included: the
# running dump stops when it finds the flag moved, and the next repeat starts
# a new one. With a printer as fast as the RP the desktop's dump takes most of
# a minute, and a held key cut it short on a real STE. With the printer on,
# the hook ignores Alt-Help while a dump runs: the job holds one whole dump,
# the same as a single quick Alt-Help's.
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/autotest.st
text "Atari +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
key f
key 0x1c
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
desktop 2500
keydown 0x38
key 0x62
keyup 0x38
jobbytes * 64026 4000
keydown 0x38
key 0x62 100
wait 200
key 0x62
keyup 0x38
jobbytes * 128052 4000
jobsame 2 job:1
